    "q-81258": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81258",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed between the curves $y=(x+2)^{2}$ and $y=2x$ from $y=0$ to $y=4.$ What is ${∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dA$ expressed as a repeated integral?",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. Writing $y=(x+2)^{2}$ and $y=2x$ in terms of $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=(x+2)^{2} & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{y}-2 \\\\ y=2x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14261987/assets/48edf4a97eb2b0c9b65eaf7bbb58757b2852b2b26f3c51177ad59899d8e40239.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\sqrt{y}-2\\le x\\le \\frac{y}{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{y}-2}^{y/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
